93\t*   **Modify:** `site/src/app/sitemap.ts`\n394\t\n395\t**2. Framework/Concepts Involved:**\n396\t*   Next.js App Router: Creating a new route segment.\n397\t*   React Server Component: The new page will be a Server Component.\n398\t*   Next.js Metadata API: To set the page `<title>`.\n399\t*   JSON-LD Schema: `FAQPage` and `HowTo` schemas for SEO.\n400\t*   Shared Components: Importing `Header` and `Footer`.\n401\t\n402\t**3. Implementation Approach:**\n403\t1.  Create `site/src/app/visa-run/page.tsx`.\n404\t2.  Define the page's `metadata` object for the title.\n405\t3.  Build the page component, importing and rendering `<Header />` and `<Footer />`.\n406\t4.  Add a `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">` tag containing a valid `FAQPage` schema with 5 placeholder questions and answers about Singapore-JB visa runs.\n407\t5.  Add a second `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">` tag for the `HowTo` schema, detailing a 5-step process for a visa run.\n408\t6.  Include a clear Call-to-Action (CTA) button or link pointing to `/book`.\n409\t7.  Edit `site/src/app/sitemap.ts` to add an entry for `/visa-run` with a `priority` of `0.85`.\n410\t\n411\t**4. Gotchas & Edge Cases:**\n412\t*   Ensure the JSON-LD content is valid and passes schema validation tools.\n413\t*   The content for the FAQ and How-To steps must be generated, as it's not in the story. It should be relevant and high-quality.\n414\t*   Verify the correct import path for the `<Footer />` component, as it may differ from the `<Header />` path.\n415\t*   The final implementation must pass `npm run build` without errors.\n416\t\n417\t## Iteration 1 - Tue, Apr 14, 2026  4:42:42 AM\n418\tFAILED diff-guard: New page: /visa-run — Dedicated Visa Run Resource Hub with FAQPage + HowTo Schema (ID: US-246) — 11574 lines > 500 limit — attempt 1/3\n419\t\n420\t\n421\t## Pre-analysis for US-246 (Gemini 2.5 Pro)\n422\tThis user story is for a Next.js/TypeScript project, not Frappe/Python. Here is the technical brief based